confirmed). **VERDICT: LADDER-TRANSFERS-A-ONLY-SUFFICIENT (bucket a)** — mere STATE-DERIVATION of controller inputs (A) survives at trained scale where §24 collapses; B+C not independently load-bearing for survival (cell1 + cell3 non_deg, cell0 + cell2 collapsed). Refines §73-FIRE / §75 stub: physics-state-AS-INPUT is the load-bearing sub-axis at trained-saturated scale, NOT the specific statistic form (moment-vs-scalar, frozen-vs-running). Critical second observation: cell2 (AB) COLLAPSES at trained scale (interval_var 0.00) — the frozen moment threshold (ema+λ·std=12.16) was tighter than real tension steady-state (~11.94 mean ± 0.07 std), so post-warmup tension rarely crosses; cell1 (A-only) succeeded with the looser frozen-mean threshold (11.945). C (time-variance) compensates by lowering effective threshold per-step (cell3 ABC). So at trained scale: A is necessary, A+frozen-mean threshold sufficient, AB-style frozen-stat-with-margin pathologically tight, full ABC robust. B-S75-FIRE 7/7 🔵 SUPPORTED-FORMAL sidecar PASS (CELL-PARTITION-EXHAUSTIVE-DISJOINT ∧ EACH-CELL-PROPER-SUBSET-§73-ABC ∧ §24-CONTROL-COLLAPSES-AT-TRAINED-FORWARD ∧ TRAINED-FORWARD-IS-REAL-NOT-STUB-NOR-TRACE ∧ WARMUP-MOMENTS-ARE-REAL-FORWARD-DERIVED ∧ CORPUS-SHA256+NO-HELPER-TOKEN ∧ SATURATION-GATE); central state/verify_hexad_blue_2026_05_15/blue_falsifier.py 0-line-diff. B-S75-FIRE-NOTE empirical carve-out (which sub-axis class survives at trained scale = SGD/measurement OUTCOME, B-D-NOTE / B-S73-FIRE-NOTE / B-S75-NOTE / B-CARVE-E6-NOTE family). Cost ≈ $0.3-0.5 runpod H100 NVL. f1/f2/f3 + B-IDENTITY-5 safe (sympy / Boolean / AST / sha256 / Kolmogorov bounded — NO σ/τ/φ/J₂ external derivation; Ψ=½ + Law-71 = anima g2 internal-arch carve-out; corpus forbidden-token grep 0). PyTorch substrate (NOT hexa-native; g_train_flame_not_pytorch evidence-anchor — anima-physics overlays on flame upstream-GAP per §71 inbox patch). north-star + §15/§51/§72 milestone UNCHANGED, GOAL 미도달. Necessary-not-sufficient 