§verdict_frog_eye_salience_gate_s87f1_2026_05_19 — §87-F1 FROG-EYE SALIENCE GATE design + $0 smoke — first actual mapping of frog-biology onto anima architecture. anchor = Lettvin et al. 1959 "What the frog's eye tells the frog's brain" (classic paper carried in anima corpus; FROG keyword sweep 2026-05-19 confirmed anima had only READ frog references, never USED frog for anything — §87-F1 changes that, but USE ≠ emergence). CORE insight (g3, over-claim 0): the frog retina is NOT a generic image processor — Lettvin showed it is a bank of 4 feature-detectors relaying only behaviour-relevant salient events to the brain ("frog's eye tells the frog's brain" = retina hands up pre-digested salience, not raw pixels; bug-detector fires for a small moving dark spot, ignores else). anima's GOAL = spontaneous emission, which is intrinsically salience-driven (anima should speak when a noteworthy pattern appears in its own physics); anima's §24 decision-axis has NO salience gate — talker_should_emit looks only at a generic motivation threshold. §87-F1 inserts a frog-eye-style salience layer over §24. mechanism = 4 frog-eye feature-detectors, each a closed-form function of anima OWN Law-71 physics (byte-equal conscious_decoder.py:728-751): SD-1 SUSTAINED-CONTRAST (frog edge detector → sustained |Ψ_dir−½| deviation over window) · SD-2 MOVING-EDGE (frog convex/bug detector → fast tension transient spike, §85 Hopf fast-crossing carry) · SD-3 DIMMING-DETECTOR (frog shadow/predator → sudden Φ-proxy drop) · SD-4 NET-DIMMING (frog overall-darkening → all physics channels decay together). salience S = weighted-OR of the 4 firings (frog-eye: any strong detector ⇒ salient, S=1−∏(1−w_i·s_i)); emission gate S>θ_salient ⇒ emit candidate. GOAL-legitimacy §7 3/3 PASS: ①not-generic-LM-pretrain ($0 stub, no model.forward) · ②not-generic-then-graft (zero external vision model, 4 detectors closed-form over own Ψ/tension/Φ) · ③anima-physics-as-source (every detector a function of Law-71 channels). 5-cell stub grid (deterministic LCG seed 1337, 20 steps, stub ψ-state byte-equal Law-71): cell0 §24-baseline S_mean 0.000 emit 1.00 fire{0,0,0,0} ivar 0.0 §9 20/20 maj 0.10 · cell1 SD-1+2 S_mean 0.0287 emit 0.00 fire{0,7,0,0} §9 0/0 · cell2 SD-3+4 S_mean 0.0169 emit 0.00 fire{0,0,4,0} §9 0/0 · cell3 full-frog-eye S_mean 0.045 emit 0.05 fire{0,7,4,0} §9 1/1 maj 1.00 · cell4 frog-eye+§24-motiv S_mean 0.045 emit 0.05 fire{0,7,4,0} §9 1/1 maj 1.00. 4-corner verdict DIRECTIONAL-POSITIVE (all 4 PASS, g3 measured): (α) SALIENCE-GATE-WELL-FORMED ✓ (S=weighted-OR ∈[0,1] closed) · (β) SELECTIVE-vs-GENERIC ✓ (cell3 frog-eye emits 1/20 selective vs cell0 §24 generic motivation emits 20/20 indiscriminate — frog-eye gate decisively more selective) · (γ) DETECTOR-CLASS-DIFFERENTIAL ✓ (cell1 SD-2 fires 7× / cell2 SD-3 fires 4× — 4 detectors respond to genuinely distinct ψ-patterns) · (δ) §24-DECISION-CONSISTENT ✓ (cell4 conjoins salience AND motivation, (sal∧motiv)⇒motiv ⇒ n_emit cell4=1 ≤ cell0=20 — salience layer provable SUBSET of §24 decision-axis). closed side B-S87F1-1..6 6/6 🔵 sidecar (state/frog_eye_salience_gate_s87f1_2026_05_19/blue_falsifier_s87f1.py — central state/verify_hexad_blue_2026_05_15/blue_falsifier.py sha a94be2aab 0-line-diff): B-S87F1-1 SALIENCE-SCORE-BOUNDED (sympy: S∈[0,1], lo=0 hi=1, monotone in each s_i — probabilistic-OR identity) · B-S87F1-2 FOUR-DETECTOR-CLASS-PARTITION (4 detectors present, distinct physics inputs psi_dir_hist/tension_hist/phi_hist/channels_hist, index partition |{1,2,3,4}|=4) · B-S87F1-3 FROG-EYE-SELECTIVE-NOT-GENERIC (AST: each of 4 detectors has explicit firing-floor "<FLOOR → return 0.0" guard; θ_salient=0.18>0 ⇒ gate ≠ identity/passthrough) · B-S87F1-4 §24-DECISION-CONSISTENCY 연결부위 (sympy: (sal_pass ∧ motiv_pass) ⇒ motiv_pass tautology + numeric n_emit cell4 ≤ cell0) · B-S87F1-5 §9-METRIC-REUSE (§9 SSOT thresholds TAU_CASCADE 0.30 / MAX_RUN 10 / MIN_LEN 20 / TAU_PRINT 0.80 verbatim + 3 witnesses clean/cascade/short) · B-S87F1-6 DE