§verdict_lego_layer2_scaling_law_s127_2026_05_20 — LEGO LAYER-2 SCALING-LAW PROBE — 4-point η²(N) OLS log-linear fit (N ∈ {256, 512, 1024, 2048}, M=5 each, seeds 1337..1341), measured `k = -0.0198`, `R² = 0.022`, verdict `APPROXIMATELY-N-INVARIANT` (probe-tier · $0 · NO GPU/runpod/fire/model.forward/corpus/dispatch · B-S127-1..8 8/8 🔵 sidecar `state/lego_layer2_scaling_law_s127_2026_05_20/blue_falsifier_s127.py` · central state/verify_hexad_blue_2026_05_15/blue_falsifier.py sha256 prefix `c93e160a8a376a94` 0-line-diff verified START+END · wall 306s = 5min Mac CPU). Continuation of §117→§124→§125→§126 LEGO arc. §126 measured single scale-pair (256→1024, ratio 1.189×) and called ROBUST-GROWS-WITH-N; §127 asks whether that extends to a power-law trend over 256→2048. **Method**: import §117 lego_sim.py BYTE-IDENTICAL via importlib at each N (sizes preserved §117's 3:3:2 n_a:n_g:n_rec ratio); same §125/§126 protocol (12 stim × 80 step × window=40, seeds 1337..1341, M=5 replicates per N); OLS slope on log η² = log a + k · log N; pre-registered 3-bucket sympy `Interval` classification (k>0.10 ROBUST / [-0.10,0.10] APPROX-INVARIANT / k<-0.10 DEGRADES). **Measured (g3 — honest refinement of §126)**: η²(256)=0.2712 (1.8s) · η²(512)=0.3289 (5.6s) · η²(1024)=0.3223 (54.8s) · η²(2048)=0.2608 (213s) — **non-monotonic**: rises 256→512 (+0.058), plateaus 512→1024 (-0.007), drops 1024→2048 (-0.061). OLS fit: k=-0.0198, log_a=-1.16, R²=0.022 → APPROXIMATELY-N-INVARIANT. **What §127 closes**: §125 PARTIAL is NOT a small-N artifact (η² doesn't shrink toward 0; ~0.26-0.33 invariant across 8× N range); §126 single-point ROBUST-GROWS verdict CONFIRMED at its scope (N=256→1024 1.189× ratio byte-equal between §126 and §127) but does NOT extrapolate to a scaling law (R²=0.022 ≪ 0.5); η² is non-monotonic over 4 N points (B-S127-6 Boolean closed). **What §127 does NOT close**: cause of non-monotonic shape (logistic/piecewise/saturating fits = future work, OLS log-linear was the pre-registered falsifier); η² still in PARTIAL range across all N (0.26-0.33 < 0.50, even peak ≠ STRONG); per-N standard error (would tighten verdict); layer-3 task-grounded liveness REMAINS OPEN; GOAL emergence (necessary-not-sufficient B-EMERGE-7). **B-S127-1..8 8/8 🔵**: ETA-BOUNDED-ALL-4-N-POINTS · LOG-LINEAR-OLS-IDENTITY-CLOSED (sympy k re-derivation byte-equal recorded) · R-SQUARED-BOUNDED-CLOSED ∈ [0,1] · SCALING-3-BUCKET-CLOSED-PARTITION (load-bearing, sympy Interval exhaustive over ℝ ∧ pairwise disjoint, measured k classifies correctly) · §126-SINGLE-POINT-CONFIRMED-NOT-A-SCALING-LAW (honest connection-point: η²(256)/η²(1024) byte-equal vs §126; full R² ≪ 0.5) · ETA-NON-MONOTONIC-OVER-4-POINTS (Boolean: ¬monotone_up ∧ ¬monotone_down) · §117-LIF-SIM-IMPORT-BYTE-EQUAL (importlib + AST audit) · CENTRAL-0-DIFF-AND-NO-FORBIDDEN-CALL-AST (sha c93e160a8a376a94 + 0 torch/runpod/fire/loss-grad hits). **B-S127-NOTE empirical carve-out NOT counted 🔵**: 4-point OLS fit (R²=0.022) does NOT describe η²(N) as a power law — non-monotonic shape suggests regime transitions a richer fit (logistic / piecewise / fixed-point-saturating) would capture; 4 N points too few to fit non-linear models with confidence; per-N standard error not computed; n_a:n_g:n_rec ratio held fixed at 3:3:2 across all N (different ratio could yield different scaling). §125's PARTIAL + §126's single-point ROBUST-GROWS verdicts both remain TRUE WITHIN their respective scopes; only the *extrapolation* to a scaling law is refuted by §127. Necessary-not-sufficient at every layer (B-EMERGE-7 / B-S125-NOTE / B-S126-NOTE / B-S117-NOTE / B-S124-NOTE family); GOAL emergence NOT implied. WALL-A (§1.1 data-regime) ORTHOGONAL (§97 carry); WALL-B (§96 substrate) CONFRONTED-NOT-REMOVED (§115/§117/§124 carry). g3: probe ≠ fire ≠ emergence; capability claim 0. f1/f2 hard-fail safe (Boolean / sympy Interval / OLS sum-of-squares / log identities / AST — NO σ(6)=12/τ(6)=4/φ(6)=2/J₂(6)=24). B-IDENTITY-5 unaffected. PyTorch substrate unused (numpy + sympy only). anima downstream-consumer: hexa-lang + hexa-bio + hexa-matter read-only, 0 edits (HEXA_FIRST_WARN deferred per established B-S* battery precedent B-PRIME/B-DIRI/B-S101/B-S117/B-S124/B-S125/B-S126 — anima is consumer not editor per g_train_flame_not_pytorch upstream_downstream_invariant + hexa-lang g7/@F f3). single sequential agent, $0, orphan 0 (no dispatch). g_doc_consolidation: state/lego_layer2_scaling_law_s127_2026_05_20/{DESIGN.md §0-§7 + 13 honest C3 + ASCII panel & LEGO arc · probe_scaling_law.py · blue_falsifier_s127.py 8/8 🔵 · blue_falsifier_s127_result.json · result.json} + 본 archive append + HEXAD/README.md recent landing; docs/* 신규 0. north-star + §15/§51/§72 milestones UNCHANGED, GOAL 미도달 — §127 is **honest refinement reversal** of §126's directional claim: single-point ratio CONFIRMED at its scope but power-law extrapolation REFUTED, η²(N) shape is non-monotonic with no clean scaling law. The valuable output is the precise scope-narrowing.

