§verdict_lego_layer2_nstim_cardinality_s131_2026_05_20 — LEGO LAYER-2 STIMULUS-CARDINALITY PROBE — orthogonal axis to §127's N-scaling; N=256 fixed, n_stim ∈ {4, 12, 24, 48}, M=5 replicates each, seeds {1337..1341}. **Measured**: η²(n_stim=4)=0.3084 / η²(12)=0.2178 / η²(24)=0.1402 / η²(48)=0.1535 — range ratio η²_max/η²_min = 0.3084/0.1402 = **2.1990×** → verdict `STRONGLY-NSTIM-DEPENDENT` (pre-registered 3-bucket sympy Interval: ratio>1.50 STRONGLY / [1.10,1.50] MILDLY / (0,1.10] INVARIANT; partition exhaustive over (0,∞) ∧ pairwise disjoint). probe-tier · $0 Mac CPU · wall 7m 14s · NO GPU/runpod/fire/model.forward/corpus/dispatch · B-S131-1..7 7/7 🔵 sidecar `state/lego_layer2_nstim_cardinality_s131_2026_05_20/blue_falsifier_s131.py` · central state/verify_hexad_blue_2026_05_15/blue_falsifier.py sha256 prefix `c93e160a8a376a94` 0-line-diff verified START+END. **First LEGO probe written against post-§129 canonical engine SSOT `HEXAD/LEGO/lego_engine.py`** (B-S131-4 AST audit: `import lego_engine` present + `importlib` NOT used + canonical engine file exists). **Key findings**: (1) **n_stim is a stronger η² modulator than N** at §117 LIF parametrisation — η² range across n_stim (2.20×) > η² range across N (1.26× from §127). (2) η² **peaks at lowest n_stim=4** (B-S131-6 Boolean closed); roughly monotone decrease 4→24, slight rise 24→48. (3) **§125's n_stim=12 was mediocre** for measuring η² — near the trough (0.218) rather than peak (0.308); arc would have called layer-2 PARTIAL more strongly at n_stim=4. (4) **Carrier capacity hypothesis** consistent (Ψ-C1 ∈ [0,1] bounded → denser stim packing dilutes between-stim signal) — consistent explanation NOT proven mechanism (honest carve-out). **What §131 does NOT close**: full η²(n_stim) curve (4 points insufficient for second-regime resolution at n_stim=24→48); peak shift at different N (would need (N, n_stim) cross matrix); layer-3 task-grounded liveness (§128 DESIGN-CLOSE carry); GOAL emergence (necessary-not-sufficient