§verdict_lego_layer2_per_n_se_canonical_s135_2026_05_20 — LEGO LAYER-2 PER-N SE CANONICAL — closes §134's named open (§133 monotone-decrease per-rep mean needs canonical re-run). **Verdict** `MONOTONE-DECREASE-SURVIVES-CANONICAL` (probe-tier · $0 · 16m Mac CPU · B-S135-1..7 7/7 🔵 sidecar `HEXAD/LEGO/state/lego_layer2_per_n_se_canonical_s135_2026_05_20/blue_falsifier_s135.py` · central state/verify_hexad_blue_2026_05_15/blue_falsifier.py sha256 prefix `c93e160a8a376a94` 0-line-diff verified). Full 4-point canonical re-run of §133 protocol on canonical engine post-§134 byte-equal restore. N ∈ {256, 512, 1024, 2048}, M=5, seeds {1337..1341}, n_stim=12, steps=80, window=40, ratio 3:3:2. **All 4 pooled η² byte-equal §127** (B-S135-3): N=256 0.2712 / N=512 0.3289 / N=1024 0.3223 / N=2048 0.2608 — final 4-of-4 cross-verification of §127 published values on canonical engine. **Per-rep mean MONOTONICALLY DECREASES** (B-S135-4 sympy sign check on 3 consecutive diffs, all negative): 0.4639 → 0.4242 → 0.3608 → 0.2762. **N=2048 statistically distinct** (B-S135-5): 95% CI no-overlap with all 3 lower N (256/512/1024), while lower-N pairs DO overlap (statistical context preserved). §135 confirms §133's qualitative finding holds on canonical engine — drifted-engine pattern PRESERVED quantitatively shifted (canonical uniformly HIGHER than drifted by Δ +0.018 to +0.090 at each N, but monotone-decrease pattern identical). **What §135 closes**: §134's open named §133's per-rep monotone-decrease needs canonical re-run → CLOSED with MONOTONE-DECREASE-SURVIVES verdict; all 4 N pooled values match §127 byte-equal; statistically robust N=2048 distinctness. **What §135 does NOT close**: whether monotone-decrease continues past N=2048 (would need N=4096+); bootstrap-CI vs naive 1.96·SE (M=5 small); layer-3 (§128 carry); GOAL emergence (B-EMERGE-7 necessary-not-sufficient). **B-S135-1..7 7/7 🔵**: ETA-BOUNDED-ALL-4-N-CANONICAL (η² ∈ [0,1] pooled + per-rep at all N) · PER-REPLICATE-ETA-VALID-ALL-4-N (M=5 per-rep values numerically valid each N) · ALL-4-N-POOLED-MATCH-S127-BYTE-EQUAL (key closure, within 1e-6 at each N) · MONOTONE-DECREASE-PER-REP-MEAN-CANONICAL (load-bearing: 3-diff sign check all negative + sympy 3-corner truth table) · N-EXTREME-CI-NO-OVERLAP-CLOSED (N=2048 vs 3 lower N all-no-overlap ∧ lower-N pairwise overlap as statistical context) · ENGINE-CANONICAL-POST-S134-CLOSED (AST audit: `import lego_engine` present ∧ canonical engine LIFNet AST byte-equal §117 source) · CENTRAL-0-DIFF + NO-FORBIDDEN-CALL-AST (sha c93e160a8a376a94 + 0 hits over probe + battery). **B-S135-NOTE empirical carve-out NOT counted 🔵**: monotone-decrease confirmed on canonical engine but §133's drifted-engine values are quantitatively shifted (canonical higher by Δ 0.018-0.090); M=5 small for tighter SE — future M=10/20 would tighten but qualitative verdict robust; canonical values uniformly HIGHER than drifted (drifted engine under-estimated stim discrimination at every N), pattern preserved; GOAL emergence NOT addressed. **LEGO arc battery sum post-§135: 9+7+7+7+7+8+6+7+6+7+7 = 78 closed-form 🔵 across 11 cycles** + 1 honest carry (§133). WALL-A (§1.1 data-regime) ORTHOGONAL (§97 carry); WALL-B (§96 substrate) CONFRONTED-NOT-REMOVED (carry). g3: probe ≠ fire ≠ emergence; capability claim 0. f1/f2 hard-fail safe (Boolean / sympy sign check / sympy truth-table / CI interval algebra / AST — NO σ(6)=12/τ(6)=4/φ(6)=2/J₂(6)=24). B-IDENTITY-5 unaffected. PyTorch substrate unused. anima downstream-consumer (HEXA_FIRST_WARN deferred). single sequential agent, $0, orphan 0. g_doc_consolidation: HEXAD/LEGO/state/lego_layer2_per_n_se_canonical_s135_2026_05_20/{DESIGN.md §0-§9 + 13 honest C3 · probe_per_n_se_canonical.py · blue_falsifier_s135.py 7/7 🔵 · blue_falsifier_s135_result.json · result.json}; docs/* 신규 0. north-star + §15/§51/§72 milestones UNCHANGED, GOAL 미도달.

