§verdict_lego_n_nstim_cross_s137_2026_05_20 — LEGO (N, n_stim) CROSS-MATRIX — 2×3 joint scaling grid N ∈ {256,1024} × n_stim ∈ {4,12,24}, M=3, canonical engine post-§134. **Verdict** `PEAK-N-STIM-N-INVARIANT` (probe-tier · $0 · 8m55s Mac CPU · B-S137-1..5 5/5 🔵 sidecar · central c93e160a8a376a94 0-line-diff). **Measured**: N=256 {n_stim4 0.3066, n_stim12 0.2930, n_stim24 0.2933} range 1.05× nearly-flat · N=1024 {n_stim4 0.5553, n_stim12 0.3510, n_stim24 0.2324} range 2.39× steep. **Two findings**: (1) peak n_stim = 4 at BOTH N (pre-registered question → PEAK-N-STIM-N-INVARIANT); (2) bonus — n_stim-gradient *steepens* with N (range 1.05×→2.39× from N=256→N=1024) = **N and n_stim are NOT separable axes, genuine interaction effect**. Carrier-capacity-dilution hypothesis (§131) strengthened: dilution is N-dependent (more units → more capacity → more sensitive to stimulus-count division). Reconciles §131 (drifted N=256 range 2.20×) / §134-revalidation (canonical N=256 incl n_stim=48 range 1.823×) / §137 (canonical N=256 n_stim∈{4,12,24} range 1.05×): the steep N=256 part is the n_stim=48 tail; within {4,12,24} N=256 is nearly flat. **B-S137-1..5 5/5 🔵**: ETA-BOUNDED-ALL-6-CELLS · PEAK-N-STIM-INVARIANT-CLOSED · NSTIM-GRADIENT-STEEPENS-WITH-N-CLOSED (range ratio N=1024 > N=256) · ENGINE-CANONICAL-POST-S134 · CENTRAL-0-DIFF + NO-FORBIDDEN-CALL-AST. B-S137-NOTE empirical carve-out (2×3 grid M=3 not full surface, NOT counted 🔵). g3: probe ≠ fire ≠ emergence; capability claim 0; necessary-not-sufficient B-EMERGE-7. WALL-A orthogonal · WALL-B confronted-not-removed. f1/f2 safe (NO σ/τ/φ/J₂). north-star + §15/§51/§72 milestones UNCHANGED, GOAL 미도달.

